{
  "information": {
    "country": "ES",
    "model_target": "euromod://ES/bsa00_es/def_const/$bsa00_amt",
    "spine_order": "49",
    "value_type": "scalar",
    "unit": "currency/year",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Basic amount"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$bsa00_amt"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$bsa00_amt is the annual \"basic amount\" of Spain's nation-wide minimum income scheme (Ingreso Mínimo Vital, IMV), defined directly within bsa00_es and set equal to 100% of the yearly non-contributory pension amount fixed each year by the government; it is the guaranteed-income reference for a single-person family unit. It feeds the Comp_perTU parameter of bsa00_es's BenCalc function (commented \"GMI amount\"), forming the base figure from which the guaranteed minimum income for the whole family unit is built, increasing by 30% for each additional member up to a ceiling, per the country report. According to the ES country report's Table 2.29, this basic amount rose from EUR 6,563.31 in 2021 to EUR 6,784.44 (2023), EUR 7,250.60 (2024) and EUR 7,905.72 (2025); the model's latest recorded value is EUR 8,803.20 per year, reflecting further annual uprating beyond the years shown in that table. The scheme was established by Real Decreto-ley 20/2020 (consolidated in Ley 19/2021, de 20 de diciembre, por la que se establece el ingreso mínimo vital)."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Policy parameters"
    },
